---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How I Helped Build the Team and Infrastructure That Brought Barstool Sports to Tampa Bay"
  description="How Pete Guzzo helped design, staff and operate Shear Media Studios — and landed Barstool Sports, Rhonda Shear's Up All Night, 30+ podcast clients and national broadcast productions in the first nine months."
  image="/images/studios/Shear-Media-Studios-Control-Room.jpg"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="cs-hero">
    <div class="cs-hero-inner">
      <a href="/work" class="cs-back">← Back to Work</a>
      <p class="cs-eyebrow">Strategy · Studio Operations · Business Development</p>
      <h1 class="cs-h1">How I Helped Build the Team and Infrastructure That Brought Barstool Sports — and Other Clients — to Tampa Bay</h1>
      <p class="cs-hero-sub">See what the market needs. Build the capability. Build the team. Then go sell it.</p>
      <div class="cs-hero-meta">
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Role</span><span class="cs-meta-val">EVP — Strategy, Studio Operations & Business Development</span></div>
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Facility</span><span class="cs-meta-val">Shear Media Studios · St. Petersburg, FL</span></div>
        <div class="cs-meta-item"><span class="cs-meta-label">Scope</span><span class="cs-meta-val">Strategy, infrastructure, operations, client development</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero-globe">
      <img src="/images/studios/SMS-SRT-Transmission-Globe.png" alt="Broadcast transmission from Tampa Bay to control rooms across the US, UK, Canada, and Australia" class="cs-globe-img" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROOF STRIP -->
  <section class="cs-proof">
    <div class="cs-proof-inner">
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">20</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Control room inputs</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">2</span><span class="cs-stat-label">VFX channels</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">0</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Missed live broadcasts</span></div>
      <div class="cs-proof-stat"><span class="cs-stat-num">4</span><span class="cs-stat-label">Countries working with</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE CAPABILITY -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The capability</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">When a client asks "Can we do this?" — I want our answer to be yes.</h2>
      <div class="cs-body-wide">
        <p class="cs-body">When I started developing the strategy for Shear Media Studios, I saw an opportunity to build something Tampa Bay needed: one connected production facility capable of serving everyone from podcasters and content creators to commercials, films, live productions and national broadcast clients.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">That meant thinking beyond individual studios.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">A roughly 15,000-square-foot production facility with multiple studios that can operate independently through their own mixers and switchers — but are also patched together through a central control room.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-cap-grid">
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Live Streaming</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Fully Capable Control Room</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Broadcast Transmission to Remote Control Rooms</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Multiple Lighting Grids + Board Control</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Multiple Studios and Sets, Independent or Together</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-cap-item">
          <span class="cs-cap-name">Podcast and Creator Environments</span>
          <span class="cs-cap-yes">Yes.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cs-cap-close">The goal was pretty simple. When a client asks, "Can we do this?" I want our answer to be yes. Then we figure out the best way to make it happen.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BUILD THE CAPABILITY FOR THE CLIENT -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Build the capability for the client</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">I don't believe in "build it and they will come."</h2>
      <div class="cs-body-wide">
        <p class="cs-body">Great movie line. Terrible sales plan.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">You have to understand what people are going to need, design for it, put the right team around it and then go sell it.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">That's what we did.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">I worked with Rhonda Shear, Van Fagan and an incredible mix of studio managers, production people, engineers, technicians, crew and partners to keep turning Shear Media Studios into one connected production operation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-pillars">
        <div class="cs-pillar">
          <h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Studio G. Studio A.</h3>
          <p class="cs-pillar-body">Multiple stages. Multiple sets. Multiple lighting grids. Independent where they need to be.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-pillar">
          <h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Podcast + Creator Environments.</h3>
          <p class="cs-pillar-body">Control. Audio. Live streaming. Broadcast transmission. Connected where they need to be.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-pillar">
          <h3 class="cs-pillar-title">Flexible for every client.</h3>
          <p class="cs-pillar-body">Never designing the entire operation around one type of client. That's what makes it work.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RHONDA SHEAR'S UP ALL NIGHT -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container cs-two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Rhonda Shear's Up All Night</p>
        <h2 class="cs-h2">Build it. Run it. Make it better.</h2>
        <p class="cs-body">One of the catalysts for putting all of this together was <strong>Rhonda Shear's Up All Night</strong>.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Before some of our larger outside clients started coming through the door, Up All Night gave us something incredibly valuable: a real show to build around, execute, correct and do again.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">We used the show to pressure-test the studio and the operation — cameras, lighting, control, audio, sets, crew communication, workflow and delivery. Not theoretically. On a real, high-quality broadcast production.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">And because it was recurring, we learned something even more valuable: <strong>working once isn't enough. It has to work again. And then better the next time.</strong></p>
        <p class="cs-body">Today, <strong>Rhonda Shear's Up All Night is on Roku</strong>, and I look at that show as one of the projects that helped us turn a collection of rooms and capabilities into an actual operating production system.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-mantra">
        <div class="cs-mantra-line">Build it.</div>
        <div class="cs-mantra-line">Run it.</div>
        <div class="cs-mantra-line">Fix it.</div>
        <div class="cs-mantra-line">Run it again.</div>
        <div class="cs-mantra-then">Then bring in the next client.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LIVE STREAMING, SRT + BROADCAST -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Live streaming, SRT + broadcast</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Talent in Tampa. Control room somewhere else. Client watching from another city. It doesn't matter.</h2>
      <div class="cs-body-wide">
        <p class="cs-body">We designed Shear Media Studios to handle both live streaming and professional broadcast transmission.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">We can stream directly to digital platforms, or cameras can originate from our studios in St. Petersburg while signals are transmitted to another control room for remote production.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Years before COVID, Gene May and I were already experimenting with giving remote clients access to the <strong style="color: var(--cs-dark-text);">actual camera feed</strong> so they could participate in a production without physically being on set.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">That stayed with me. When we started developing Shear, my thinking was simple:</p>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="cs-pull-quote">
        If our cameras can talk to our control room, our control room should be able to talk to another control room anywhere.
      </blockquote>
      <p class="cs-body">We built that capability before knowing exactly who would need it. Then somebody did.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AND THEN BARSTOOL SHOWED UP -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">And then Barstool showed up</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Within our first nine months, I got the opportunity to bid on a recurring Barstool Sports professional football production.</h2>
      <div class="cs-two-col cs-barstool-cols">
        <div>
          <p class="cs-body">Custom set in Studio G. Six cameras. Weekly live production. Remote control room. Broadcast transmission.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">Suddenly capabilities we'd been developing "just in case" had exactly the kind of client we'd been preparing for.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">So I sold it. Then we had to make the damn thing work.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">During one of our first transmission tests, we hit a network problem involving routing, port forwarding and SRT. Five engineers were waiting on the other end.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <blockquote class="cs-pull-quote-light">
            I'm not a network engineer. I'm the guy who helped sell the production and needed the network to work.
          </blockquote>
          <p class="cs-body">Fortunately, I'd spent months on nights and weekends building AI agents and developing CORTEX specifically to help me attack problems I didn't already know how to solve.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">I paired those tools with Codex, dug into the network documentation and architecture, learned what I needed in real time and worked the problem with the team.</p>
          <p class="cs-body">Signals connected. Test cleared. Show live. Then we did it again the next week.</p>
          <p class="cs-body cs-missed-zero"><strong>Missed broadcasts: zero.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NINE MONTHS. A LOT MORE THAN ONE CLIENT. -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark">
    <div class="cs-container">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">Nine months. A lot more than one client.</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2">Barstool is a great win. But it's one piece of what we've built.</h2>
      <div class="cs-result-grid">
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">Rhonda Shear — Up All Night</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Original entertainment production starring Rhonda Shear and now available on Roku. It also became one of the catalysts that helped us develop, test and refine the production operation we're using today.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">Barstool Sports</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Recurring national sports production. Custom Studio G set. Six-camera workflow. Live production with remote broadcast control and transmission.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">30+ Podcast Clients + Content Creators</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Creators, businesses and personalities using different configurations throughout the facility — from intimate podcast environments to larger produced shows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">Commercials + Branded Content</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Major commercial and branded productions using our stages, sets, crews and connected production infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-block">
          <h3 class="cs-result-title">Film + Specialty Series</h3>
          <p class="cs-body">Film, episodic and specialty productions using Shear Media Studios as more than a stage — as a production home.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ONE BUILDING. ONE CONNECTED PRODUCTION OPERATION. -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-light">
    <div class="cs-container cs-two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">One building. One connected production operation.</p>
        <h2 class="cs-h2">That's the part of Shear Media Studios I'm probably most proud of.</h2>
        <p class="cs-body">It isn't just the technology. And it isn't just the rooms. It's how everything works together.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">We're still building. We're developing more multi-set configurations in Studio A, expanding our podcast environments and finding new ways for productions to move between spaces and control points.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Every client teaches us something. How crews move. Where people naturally work. What clients ask for. What needs to connect. What we should build next.</p>
        <p class="cs-body">Because you don't really finish designing a production studio when construction ends.</p>
        <p class="cs-body"><strong>The people using it help you finish it.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <ul class="cs-connected-list">
        <li>Multiple studios</li>
        <li>Multiple sets</li>
        <li>Multiple lighting grids</li>
        <li>Individual mixers and switchers</li>
        <li>Central control</li>
        <li>Podcast environments</li>
        <li>Live streaming</li>
        <li>SRT</li>
        <li>Broadcast transmission</li>
        <li class="cs-connected-last">A team that knows how to make all of it work</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STRATEGY -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark cs-strategy-section">
    <div class="cs-container cs-strategy-inner">
      <p class="cs-section-eyebrow">The strategy</p>
      <h2 class="cs-h2 cs-strategy-h2">I didn't help design Shear Media Studios for Barstool Sports. I helped design an operation where a Barstool Sports could happen.</h2>
      <p class="cs-body">And Rhonda Shear's Up All Night. And a podcast. And a commercial. And a film. And whatever walks through the door next.</p>
      <p class="cs-body">That's what this has really been about from the beginning.</p>
      <div class="cs-strategy-lines">
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">See what the market needs.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">Build the capability.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">Build the team.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line">Sell it.</div>
        <div class="cs-strategy-line cs-strategy-last">Then keep making it better.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cs-section cs-dark cs-cta-section">
    <div class="cs-container cs-cta-inner">
      <h2 class="cs-cta-head">Need someone who can think like this and build like this?</h2>
      <p class="cs-cta-sub">Strategy, infrastructure, operations, client development — or all four. Let's talk.</p>
      <div class="cs-cta-btns">
        <a href="/contact" class="cs-btn-primary">Talk to Pete →</a>
        <a href="https://www.shearmediastudios.com/live-transmission" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cs-btn-secondary">See Shear Media Studios →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ─── TOKENS ─── */
  :root {
    --cs-ink: #1c1917;
    --cs-paper: #f5f0eb;
    --cs-rust: #9b4a2a;
    --cs-dark-bg: #0d0f14;
    --cs-dark-surface: #151820;
    --cs-dark-border: rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
    --cs-dark-text: #e8e2da;
    --cs-dark-muted: rgba(232,226,218,0.60);
    --cs-accent: #5ea8e6;
    --cs-accent-warm: #f1f6a4;
    --cs-container: 72rem;
    --cs-px: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  /* ─── HERO ─── */
  .cs-hero {
    background: var(--cs-dark-bg);
    color: var(--cs-dark-text);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    max-width: var(--cs-container);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem var(--cs-px) 5rem;
  }
  .cs-back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--cs-dark-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .cs-back:hover { color: var(--cs-dark-text); }
  .cs-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--cs-accent-warm);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .cs-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.2vw, 2.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .cs-hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--cs-accent-warm);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .cs-hero-meta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-meta-item { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .cs-meta-label { color: var(--cs-accent); font-weight: 600; min-width: 4rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.7rem; padding-top: 0.05rem; }
  .cs-meta-val { color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }
  .cs-hero-globe { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .cs-globe-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 480px;
    mix-blend-mode: lighten;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, #000 58%, transparent 72%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, #000 58%, transparent 72%);
  }

  /* ─── PROOF STRIP ─── */
  .cs-proof {
    background: var(--cs-dark-surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border);
  }
  .cs-proof-inner {
    max-width: var(--cs-container);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem var(--cs-px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cs-proof-stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .cs-stat-num { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 3rem); color: #fff; line-height: 1.15; }
  .cs-stat-label { font-size: 0.7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--cs-accent-warm); text-wrap: balance; }

  /* ─── SECTIONS ─── */
  .cs-section { padding: 5rem 0; }
  .cs-light { background: var(--cs-paper); color: var(--cs-ink); }
  .cs-dark { background: var(--cs-dark-bg); color: var(--cs-dark-text); }
  .cs-container { max-width: var(--cs-container); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--cs-px); }
  .cs-section-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .cs-light .cs-section-eyebrow { color: var(--cs-rust); }
  .cs-dark .cs-section-eyebrow { color: var(--cs-accent-warm); }
  .cs-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.8vw, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .cs-light .cs-h2 { color: var(--cs-ink); }
  .cs-dark .cs-h2 { color: #fff; }
  .cs-body { font-size: 0.975rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .cs-light .cs-body { color: rgba(28,25,23,0.75); }
  .cs-dark .cs-body { color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }
  .cs-body-wide { max-width: 46rem; }

  /* ─── TWO-COL ─── */
  .cs-two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4rem; align-items: center; }
  .cs-img-block { border-radius: 0.5rem; overflow: hidden; }
  .cs-img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }

  /* ─── PILLARS ─── */
  .cs-pillars { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .cs-pillar { border-top: 2px solid var(--cs-dark-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-n { font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--cs-accent); font-weight: 700; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-title { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .cs-pillar-body { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--cs-dark-muted); }

  /* ─── RESULT GRID ─── */
  .cs-result-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .cs-result-block { border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); padding-top: 1.5rem; }
  .cs-result-title { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--cs-accent-warm); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }

  /* ─── CTA ─── */
  .cs-cta-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); }
  .cs-cta-inner { text-align: center; padding: 5rem var(--cs-px); max-width: var(--cs-container); margin: 0 auto; }
  .cs-cta-head { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.8vw, 2.5rem); color: #fff; margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 36rem; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .cs-cta-sub { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--cs-dark-muted); max-width: 32rem; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .cs-cta-btns { display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cs-btn-primary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0.875rem 2rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; background: var(--cs-paper); color: var(--cs-ink); text-decoration: none; transition: background 0.2s; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  .cs-btn-primary:hover { background: #fff; }
  .cs-btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0.875rem 2rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid var(--cs-dark-border); color: var(--cs-dark-text); text-decoration: none; transition: border-color 0.2s; }
  .cs-btn-secondary:hover { border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); }

  /* ─── CAPABILITY GRID ─── */
  .cs-cap-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.12);
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .cs-cap-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 1.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.08);
    border-right: 1px solid rgba(28,25,23,0.08);
  }
  .cs-cap-item:nth-child(3n) { border-right: none; padding-right: 0; }
  .cs-cap-name {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: rgba(28,25,23,0.45);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .cs-cap-yes {
    font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    color: var(--cs-rust);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .cs-cap-close {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: rgba(28,25,23,0.5);
    font-style: italic;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  /* ─── MANTRA ─── */
  .cs-mantra {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    align-self: center;
  }
